  "authentication_contract": "Only recent-dispositions GET changes to Bearer alerts:read, tenant intersection and explicit RLS. Separate per-tenant AISOC_TRIAGE_DISPOSITIONS_KEYS_FILE with no shared-token fallback; prior six org-memory, skill and KB reader identities/env/mounts remain unchanged.",
  "cutoff_contract": "Original table has created_at NOT NULL but no updated_at/history or UPDATE prohibition. The cutoff only checks recorded creation time; it cannot reconstruct subsequently edited historical notes. Frozen reader validates echo and row timestamps and rejects unhonoured cutoffs without double-counting exclusions. Missing-time fixture is unit/projection only.",
  "adoption_contract": "Preserves same-rule priority, then creation time; ID adds a deterministic tie-break only. Response identity/hash and rule/entity match basis are distinct from sanitized adopted text/hash and final prompt block/hash. Typed status, reason, HTTP, identity/query/URL-bound cache and counts persist. Mapping is checked before cache; failed refresh adopts no stale decisions.",
  "containment_contract": "Preserves top5, note240 and the existing disposition-block3000-character budget. Complete heading/personal-opinion advisory and exact adopted rows are budgeted and sanitized once. Model literal cap8000 and shared system prompt/registry/lock remain unchanged. Historical opinions are not current authorization or evidence.",
  "projection_hash_contract": "row_source_sha256 hashes only the canonical API row projection plus scoped tenant_id (sorted compact UTF8 JSON); not the complete database row, historical version proof or authentication signature.",
  "persistence_contract": "recent_dispositions_read is included in the existing verdict first-write transaction and independent artifact. Artifact error rolls back and typed failure propagates; retry does not duplicate original event/artifact. Generic Run/alert retry behavior is unchanged.",
  "fixture_contract": "Five marked synthetic feedback rows in existing A/B test tenants, with nullable alert_id and retained NOT NULL/FK constraints; only read semantics, not analyst write/compiler/closure acceptance. One natural R-DISP-A model fixture matches feedback and naturally has no old skill selection or KB match; the three previous readers are separately checked with their original queries.",
  "scope_limitations": [
    "Default120-second cache does not instantly observe server revocation or edits.",
    "Identity reader remains separate work; resident worker, graph, approvals and real responses stay disabled.",
    "One actual model response cannot accept full classification, historical-feedback or investigation quality."
  ]
}
